THE A1.3 FIX (loader.go:1080). The buggy line was
`if pair.Left.Hash == decision.SuppressedHash`; SuppressedHash is rekeyed to a StableID on
save (duplicate_decisions.go:107-108 canonicalKey + writeDecisionsLocked:154-172), so a
legacy content hash can never equal it and the Left=kept/Right=suppressed role swap never
fired. The fix introduces identityMatchesSuppressed (stable_id.go:41-49) which matches
EITHER key form: `t.StableID != "" && key == t.StableID` then `key == t.Hash`. This handles
both stored forms: a StableID SuppressedHash (post-A1 normal case, proven by the A1.3
regression test) and a legacy-hash SuppressedHash (pre-A1 / out-of-range row where
canonicalKey is a no-op; the `key == t.Hash` branch covers it — verified with a throwaway
test in /tmp/a1_revert that passes for the legacy form even under the buggy comparison
because legacy==legacy, and the fixed code satisfies it via the same branch).

REGRESSION TEST GENUINELY FAILS WITHOUT THE FIX. Copied the repo to /tmp/a1_revert,
reverted ONLY the loader.go fix (restored `if pair.Left.Hash == decision.SuppressedHash`,
dropped the helper call + comment), left the new test in place, ran:
  go test ./internal/services/dataloader/ -run TestApplyDuplicateDetection_SuppressEarlierInFile_KeptIsLeft
Result: FAIL — `resolved Left = "2b0d013a1d6966cf" ("Lucid"), want the KEPT check
"78aa352ca55d57de"` and `resolved Right = "78aa352ca55d57de" ("Check #996683"), want the
SUPPRESSED bill pay`. Roles inverted exactly as the defect describes. With the fix in the
main tree the same test PASSES. The test drives the PUBLIC write path and calls LoadData
(stable_id_test.go:532) BEFORE SaveDuplicateDecision (:560), so the stableIDIndex is
populated and canonicalKey rekeys the posted hashes — the real /duplicates flow. Without
that ordering canonicalKey is a no-op and the bug hides; the test enforces it.

